ttitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn6le03ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " How Much or How Many?", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use quantifiers to express quantities and amounts. There are various quantifiers you can use to express a small amount or a large amount.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use quantifiers with both count and non-count nouns.  You can use all of the quantifiers below with both count and non-count nouns.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Quantifier\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"more<br />  less/fewer<br /> no/none<br /> any /not any<br /> some<br /> a lot of/lots of<br /> plenty of<br /> enough\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a larger number/amount<br /> a smaller number/amount<br /> 0, nothing<br /> ask about a number or amount/say there is no<br /> a small number/amount<br /> a very large number/amount<br /> more than you need<br /> as much as you need\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Measurements (Nouns)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Amount\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"pound<br />pint<br />  quart<br />   dozen<br /> slice<br />  case\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a little less than half a kilogram at 454 g<br /> a little less than half a liter<br /> a little less than one liter<br /> 12 pieces<br /> a cut piece from a whole<br /> a paper case of 6, 12 or 24 bottles\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Vanessa needs to cook a pound of chicken for the meal.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Sally brought a quart of ice cream. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Peter brought a half dozen pieces of naan.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Is it necessary?", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " \u201c<span class=\"strong\">Have got</span> to\u201d is used to express necessity. It is more commonly used in British English. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " \u201c<span class=\"strong\">Have got</span> to\u201d has irregular forms in the past and future. Look at the chart below.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":5,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Subject <br/>I/You/We/They</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">+ <span class=\\\"strong\\\">have got</span> to<br/><span class=\\\"strong\\\">'ve got</span> to</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+  verb in base form (infinitive)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+  complement\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Subject <br/>He/She</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">+ <span class=\\\"strong\\\">has got</span> to<br/><span class=\\\"strong\\\">'s got</span> to</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+  verb in base form (infinitive)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+  complement\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Past</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Subject</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">+ <span class=\\\"strong\\\">had</span> to</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+  verb in base form (infinitive)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+  complement\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Future</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Subject</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+ will + <span class=\\\"strong\\\">have</span> + to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+  verb in base form (infinitive)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+  complement\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Examples:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Future\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You have got to finish your homework tonight.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I had to finish your homework last night.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You will have to finish your homework tonight.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" We've got to arrive early to get seats.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" We had to arrive early to get seats.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" We will have to arrive early to get seats.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You've got to wash your hands before you start cooking.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I had to wash my hands before I started cooking.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You will have to wash your hands before you start cooking.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You must serve the food as soon as it's ready.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I had to serve the food as soon as it was ready.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I will have to serve the food as soon as it is ready.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"What have you got to do there?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"What did you have to do there?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"What will you have to do there?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about food and cooking.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "pint", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a measurement used in the US and the UK equal to almost 500 milliliters", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Peter brought a pint of yogurt to help soften the spicy taste.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le03ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "quart", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a measurement used in the US and the UK equal to almost 1 liter ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sally brought a quart of mango ice cream for dessert.", "type": "example"}, {"con